In error message this is the key: " 23 oom-kill event(s) in StepId=33165689.batch. Some of your processes may have been killed by the cgroup out-of-memory handler. "
when parallelizing the permutation, after spinning ~10th task, the node ran out of memory and all the rest failed (23 out-of-memory events).

You can normally control this by limiting the number of cores (so instead of all available cores, use 8 for example). I am not sure if the PARALLEL option lm.rrpp exposes that setting though.

